From 273720ad5f29e563995053eed274d1b43011f52f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@lccc.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] x86-64: compare-replay from register homes via RA
 interval extension (IS-07/IS-09)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Compare-replay — the Cmp skips setcc/movzbl entirely and its Select/
CondBranch consumer re-emits the compare from recorded operands right
before the cmov/jcc — was restricted to SLOT-homed operands ever since
the sqlite3 yy_shift miscompile: a register-homed operand's live range
ended at the ORIGINAL Cmp position, the allocator freed the register, a
later-defined value reused it, and the replayed compare read the wrong
value (state+415 instead of state).

The real defect was a missing RA contract, not the mechanism: the
backend reads the operands at the CONSUMER position, and nothing told
the allocator. This commit supplies that contract through the existing
folded_index_uses channel (whose documented semantics — "the backend
reads this value at the consumer's position" — cover replay exactly):

* The replay candidate scan moves to
  comparison::compute_cmp_replay_scan, a pure IR function consumed by
  BOTH the prologue (emitter contract) and the RA-link builder — the
  allocator and emitter can never disagree about which operands are
  read where. Each link maps an operand value to its Cmp DEST, whose
  single use IS the consumer: extending the operand's interval to the
  dest's end covers the replay position precisely.

* The pre-RA scan accepts every Value operand optimistically; the
  home decision moves to post-RA pruning with homes final:
  pre-existing slot -> always safe; register assignment -> safe under
  the interval extension (refused when CCC_NO_FOLDED_INDEX_LIVENESS
  disables it); neither home -> safe only if the allocator will grant a
  spill slot; never-materialized values prune the entry (the Cmp then
  materializes its boolean normally — fallback, never miscompile).

Results: `x > hi ? hi : x` chains now replay the second compare from
register homes — clamp emits cmp/cmovg/cmpl/cmovl where it emitted
setl+movzbl+testq+cmovne (4 instructions saved per clamp link); the
sqlite hazard shape replays off a register the RA provably keeps (the
add is steered to a scratch). Census: 6278 -> 6258 instructions vs GCC
5773; gzip_crc32 and zlib_ng_adler32 each shed further instructions.

Validated: exhaustive clamp (11^3 input space) and state-select
(-100..800 strided) suites bit-identical to GCC; lib gate 1302/0 under
-D warnings; x86-64 regression corpus 966/0 (sqlite corpus tests
included); i686 failure set unchanged; godbolt x86-64 census improved
with no per-program regressions.
